            <div type="translation" xml:lang="en" resp="#AA">
                <p>
                    To Nero [Claudius, son of the divine Claudius], [grandson] of Germanicus Caesar, [great-grandson of Tiberius Caesar Augustus], [great-great-grandson] of the deified Augustus, 
                    [Caesar Augustus] Germanicus, pontifex maximus, holder of tribunician power for the [11th?] time, [imperator for the 9th? time, consul for the 4th time], 
                    [Lucius Titinius Glaucius] Lucretianus [son of Lucius, of tribe Galeria] duovir, [quinquennial quattuorvir, appointed first by the] favour of the Deified Claudius, 
                    [prefect of Nero Claudius Caesar Augustus, patron] of the colony, sevir of the Roman equites, [curio for performing sacred rites, flamen of Roma], flamen of Augustus, 
                    [appointed] by the favour [of Caesar], [military tribune for the] 22nd [legion] Primigenia, [prefect of the] Balaeric [islands], [dedicates this] in performance [of a vow].  
                </p>
            </div>
            <div type="commentary">
                <p>This is the same Lucius Titinius Glaucus Lucretianus as in <ref target="EmpWor000476">EmpWor000476</ref> and <ref target="EmpWor000477">EmpWor000477</ref> both from Luna (It. VII), and in CIL 11.1332 and CIL 11.1349a (both from Luna, It. VII). He may also be attested in <ref target="EmpWor000451">EmpWor000451</ref> from Cosa (It. VII).</p> 
            </div>
